{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789949666,"nonce":"kRGLUSvu4tfaqFloBcYX2RXMNlI=","title":"A call through a Dynamic-typed function value passes raw arguments and reads a raw result","message":"static function applyDyn(f, x, y) return f(x, y);   // f, x, y unannotated -\u003e Dynamic\n    applyDyn(compare, 5, 2)     // SIGSEGV (Haxe: 3)\n    applyDyn((a, b) -\u003e a - b, 5, 2)   // 16 (Haxe: 3)\n\n`lower_indirect_call` with a callee whose type is Dynamic builds the call\nsignature from the argument registers and reads the result as\n`convert_type(expr.ty)` = Ptr(Void). A lambda or the closure-value adapter\nis `(env, declared..) -\u003e declared`, so an Int result is read as a box\npointer and a boxed argument as an Int.\n\nDesign: every closure target (lambda, closure-value adapter, method-ref\nthunk, inner function) gets an erased entry `(env, box..) -\u003e box` that\nunboxes each argument to the declared type and boxes the result; module\ninit registers `(typed code ptr -\u003e entry)` through closure records\n(`IrValue::Function` is not lowered by the LLVM backend, records are);\na Dynamic call site boxes every argument, asks the runtime for the entry\nview of the closure (`{entry, env}`, or the closure itself when none is\nregistered) and calls with `(ptr..) -\u003e ptr`. The runtime array helpers\n(`haxe_array_map`/`filter`/`sort`, ereg map) assume `(env, i64..) -\u003e i64`\nand break on f64 parameters (`[2.0, 4.0].map(half)` -\u003e `0,0`); a second,\nslot-shaped entry `(env, i64..) -\u003e i64` looked up by fn_ptr fixes those\nwithout touching their loops.\n\nScratchpad probes: S3.hx (applyDyn), D1.hx (callit), M1.hx (Float map).","files":null}]}